/-!
# Capped Floer coefficients on complex projective space

This file computes the coefficient and capping data of capped Hamiltonian Floer theory on complex
projective space `CPⁿ`, `n ≥ 1`, the target of the quantum relation `x^(n+1) = q^[line]`. Let
`ω : H₂(CPⁿ; ℤ) →+ ℝ` and `c : H₂(CPⁿ; ℤ) →+ ℤ` be homomorphisms, for the symplectic area and the
first Chern number. Since `CPⁿ` is simply connected, every class of `H₂(CPⁿ; ℤ)` is spherical
(`TauCeti.sphericalClasses_eq_top_of_simplyConnectedSpace`), and `H₂(CPⁿ; ℤ)` is generated by the
Hurewicz class of the generator of `π₂(CPⁿ) ≅ ℤ`
(`TauCeti.ComplexProjectiveSpace.zmultiples_hurewiczIntHom_pi2MulEquivInt_symm`); at the base
point `[e₁]` this generator is the class of the coordinate line with its complex orientation
(`TauCeti.ComplexProjectiveSpace.pi2MulEquivInt_symm_ofAdd_one`). So `ω` and `c` are determined by
their values on this class. For the Fubini–Study form and the first Chern class of `CPⁿ` these
are the area of a line and `n + 1`.

* **The period group.** The class `ℓ = SphericalPeriodGroup.projectiveSpaceGenerator ω c v hn` of
  the generator of `π₂(CPⁿ)` at a base point `[v]` generates the period group
  `Γ = SphericalPeriodGroup ω c` (`SphericalPeriodGroup.zmultiples_projectiveSpaceGenerator`), so
  `Γ` is cyclic for every `n`. It is trivial exactly when both periods of `ℓ` vanish
  (`SphericalPeriodGroup.subsingleton_projectiveSpace_iff`), and otherwise the class map is an
  isomorphism `H₂(CPⁿ; ℤ) ≅ Γ`
  (`SphericalPeriodGroup.ofSingularHomology_projectiveSpace_bijective`).
* **Monotonicity and Laurent coefficients.** When `c ℓ ≠ 0`, `CPⁿ` is spherically monotone,
  `ω = τ c` on spherical classes with `τ = ω ℓ / c ℓ`
  (`SphericalPeriodGroup.area_eq_mul_chern_projectiveSpace`). If `ω ℓ` and `c ℓ` are positive,
  `ℓ` is the positive Chern generator
  (`SphericalPeriodGroup.chernEquivInt_projectiveSpaceGenerator`), and the Floer Novikov ring is
  the ring of formal Laurent series in the variable `X = e^(-ℓ)`
  (`TauCeti.Floer.NovikovRing.toLaurentSeries_single_neg_zsmul_projectiveSpaceGenerator`), of raw
  degree `-2 c ℓ` and valuation `ω ℓ`.
* **The coefficient comparison `q^A ↦ e^(-A)`.** Unless both periods of `ℓ` vanish, the
  comparison `TauCeti.Floer.coefficientComparison` from the Novikov ring indexed by the class
  group `H₂(CPⁿ; ℤ)` of genus-zero Gromov–Witten theory to the Floer Novikov ring is bijective
  (`TauCeti.Floer.coefficientComparison_ofSingularHomology_projectiveSpace_bijective`), and in
  Laurent coordinates it sends `q^(k [ℓ])` to `X^k`
  (`TauCeti.Floer.NovikovRing.toLaurentSeries_coefficientComparison_projectiveSpace_single`). In
  particular `q^ℓ` is the Laurent variable `X`. This is the class `q^[line]` of the quantum
  relation: on `CPⁿ⁺¹`, based at `[e₁] = [0 : 1 : 0 : ⋯ : 0]`, `ℓ` is the class of the coordinate
  line with its complex orientation
  (`SphericalPeriodGroup.projectiveSpaceGenerator_eq_ofHomotopyGroup_lineSquare`).
  The comparison preserves degrees: a nonzero monomial `r e^(k ℓ)` has raw degree `2 k c ℓ` and
  no other
  (`TauCeti.Floer.NovikovRing.single_zsmul_projectiveSpaceGenerator_mem_gradeBy_degree_iff`), so
  `q^(k [ℓ])`, of quantum degree `2 k c ℓ`, goes to a series of raw degree `-2 k c ℓ`, that is
  of cochain degree `2 k c ℓ`
  (`TauCeti.Floer.coefficientComparison_projectiveSpace_single_mem_gradeBy_degree`). For
  `c ℓ = n + 1` and `k = 1` this is the degree `2 n + 2` of `x^(n+1)`.
* **Recapping.** On every loop of `CPⁿ` the cap classes form a `Γ`-torsor, and unless both periods
  of `ℓ` vanish any two caps differ by recapping with a unique multiple `k • ℓ`
  (`SphericalCapClass.existsUnique_zsmul_projectiveSpaceGenerator_vadd_eq`), which raises the
  action by `k ω ℓ` and the grading by `2 k c ℓ`.

These are the specializations to `CPⁿ` of the results on period groups generated by one sphere in
`TauCeti.Geometry.Symplectic.Floer.SphericalPeriodGroup`, which also cover the two-sphere
(`TauCeti.Geometry.Symplectic.Floer.Examples.Sphere`). The homomorphisms `ω` and `c` are
arbitrary: identifying them with the integrals of the Fubini–Study form and the first Chern class
of `CPⁿ` is not done here.

## References

* H. Hofer and D. A. Salamon, *Floer homology and Novikov rings*, in *The Floer memorial
  volume*, Progr. Math. 133 (1995), 483–524.
* D. McDuff and D. Salamon, *J-holomorphic curves and symplectic topology*, Section 11.1, on the
  Novikov ring of a symplectic manifold and the quantum cohomology of `CPⁿ`.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open AlgebraicTopology CategoryTheory HomotopyGroup Metric
open scoped Topology.Homotopy

namespace TauCeti.Floer

open NovikovSeries PeriodGroup TauCeti.ComplexProjectiveSpace

variable {n : ℕ}
  {ω : ((singularHomologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{0} ℤ) 2).obj (ModuleCat.of ℤ ℤ)).obj
    (TopCat.of (ComplexProjectiveSpace n)) →+ ℝ}
  {c : ((singularHomologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{0} ℤ) 2).obj (ModuleCat.of ℤ ℤ)).obj
    (TopCat.of (ComplexProjectiveSpace n)) →+ ℤ}

namespace SphericalPeriodGroup

/-- The period group of `CPⁿ` is cyclic, for every `n`: for `n ≥ 1` it is generated by the class of
the generator of `π₂(CPⁿ)`, and `CP⁰` is a point. -/
instance : IsAddCyclic (SphericalPeriodGroup ω c) := by
  rcases eq_or_ne n 0 with rfl | hn'
  · have : Subsingleton (SphericalPeriodGroup ω c) :=
      subsingleton_of_forall_subsingleton fun _ => inferInstance
    infer_instance
  · obtain ⟨v', -⟩ := mk_surjective n (Classical.arbitrary (ComplexProjectiveSpace n))
    exact isAddCyclic_of_zmultiples_eq_top
      (zmultiples_hurewiczIntHom_pi2MulEquivInt_symm v' hn')

variable (v : sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℂ (Fin (n + 1))) 1) (hn : n ≠ 0)

variable (ω c) in
/-- **The class of the generator of `π₂(CPⁿ)`** in the period group of `CPⁿ`, `n ≥ 1`: the class of
the element of `π₂(CPⁿ, [v])` sent to `1` by
`TauCeti.ComplexProjectiveSpace.pi2MulEquivInt`. At the base point `[e₁]` of `CPⁿ⁺¹` it is the
class of the coordinate line with its complex orientation
(`SphericalPeriodGroup.projectiveSpaceGenerator_eq_ofHomotopyGroup_lineSquare`). It generates the
period group
(`SphericalPeriodGroup.zmultiples_projectiveSpaceGenerator`). -/
def projectiveSpaceGenerator : SphericalPeriodGroup ω c :=
  ofHomotopyGroup ω c (mk n v)
    (Additive.ofMul ((pi2MulEquivInt v hn).symm (Multiplicative.ofAdd 1)))

/-- The generator is the class `ofHomotopyGroup` of the generator of `π₂(CPⁿ)`, so the general
results on period groups generated by one sphere apply to it. -/
theorem projectiveSpaceGenerator_def :
    projectiveSpaceGenerator ω c v hn =
      ofHomotopyGroup ω c (mk n v)
        (Additive.ofMul ((pi2MulEquivInt v hn).symm (Multiplicative.ofAdd 1))) :=
  (rfl)

/-- **Classes of `H₂(CPⁿ; ℤ)` in the period group**: the Hurewicz class of the generator of
`π₂(CPⁿ)` is sent to the generator `ℓ`, so the class of `k` times it is `k • ℓ`. Not a simp
lemma: simp already rewrites its left-hand side by
`SphericalPeriodGroup.ofSingularHomology_hurewiczIntHom`. -/
theorem ofSingularHomology_hurewiczIntHom_pi2MulEquivInt_symm :
    ofSingularHomology ω c (sphericalClasses_eq_top_of_simplyConnectedSpace _)
        (hurewiczIntHom _ (mk n v) 1
          (Additive.ofMul ((pi2MulEquivInt v hn).symm (Multiplicative.ofAdd 1)))) =
      projectiveSpaceGenerator ω c v hn :=
  ofSingularHomology_hurewiczIntHom _ _ _

/-- The area of the generator is the value of `ω` on its Hurewicz class. -/
@[simp]
theorem area_projectiveSpaceGenerator :
    PeriodGroup.area _ _ (projectiveSpaceGenerator ω c v hn) =
      ω (hurewiczIntHom _ (mk n v) 1
        (Additive.ofMul ((pi2MulEquivInt v hn).symm (Multiplicative.ofAdd 1)))) := by
  simp [projectiveSpaceGenerator]

/-- The first Chern number of the generator is the value of `c` on its Hurewicz class. -/
@[simp]
theorem chern_projectiveSpaceGenerator :
    PeriodGroup.chern _ _ (projectiveSpaceGenerator ω c v hn) =
      c (hurewiczIntHom _ (mk n v) 1
        (Additive.ofMul ((pi2MulEquivInt v hn).symm (Multiplicative.ofAdd 1)))) := by
  simp [projectiveSpaceGenerator]

/-- **The generator of `π₂(CPⁿ)` generates the period group of `CPⁿ`.** -/
theorem zmultiples_projectiveSpaceGenerator :
    AddSubgroup.zmultiples (projectiveSpaceGenerator ω c v hn) = ⊤ :=
  zmultiples_ofHomotopyGroup_eq_top (zmultiples_hurewiczIntHom_pi2MulEquivInt_symm v hn)

/-- **The period group of `CPⁿ` is trivial exactly when both periods of the generator
vanish.** -/
theorem subsingleton_projectiveSpace_iff :
    Subsingleton (SphericalPeriodGroup ω c) ↔
      PeriodGroup.area _ _ (projectiveSpaceGenerator ω c v hn) = 0 ∧
        PeriodGroup.chern _ _ (projectiveSpaceGenerator ω c v hn) = 0 :=
  subsingleton_iff_of_zmultiples_eq_top
    (zmultiples_hurewiczIntHom_pi2MulEquivInt_symm v hn)

/-- **On `CPⁿ` the class map `H₂(CPⁿ; ℤ) → Γ` is an isomorphism** unless both periods of the
generator vanish. -/
theorem ofSingularHomology_projectiveSpace_bijective
    (h : PeriodGroup.area _ _ (projectiveSpaceGenerator ω c v hn) ≠ 0 ∨
      PeriodGroup.chern _ _ (projectiveSpaceGenerator ω c v hn) ≠ 0) :
    Function.Bijective
      (ofSingularHomology ω c (sphericalClasses_eq_top_of_simplyConnectedSpace _)) :=
  ⟨ofSingularHomology_injective_of_zmultiples_eq_top
    (zmultiples_hurewiczIntHom_pi2MulEquivInt_symm v hn) _ h,
    ofSingularHomology_surjective _⟩

/-- **`CPⁿ` is spherically monotone** when the Chern number of the generator is nonzero: on
spherical classes `ω = τ c` with `τ = ω ℓ / c ℓ`. This is the hypothesis of the monotone Laurent
model `TauCeti.Floer.NovikovRing.toLaurentSeries`. -/
theorem area_eq_mul_chern_projectiveSpace
    (h : PeriodGroup.chern _ _ (projectiveSpaceGenerator ω c v hn) ≠ 0)
    (s : sphericalClasses (ComplexProjectiveSpace n) 1) :
    ω.comp (sphericalClasses _ 1).subtype s =
      PeriodGroup.area _ _ (projectiveSpaceGenerator ω c v hn) /
          PeriodGroup.chern _ _ (projectiveSpaceGenerator ω c v hn) *
        c.comp (sphericalClasses _ 1).subtype s :=
  area_eq_mul_chern_of_zmultiples_eq_top
    (zmultiples_hurewiczIntHom_pi2MulEquivInt_symm v hn) h s

section Laurent

variable (hker : (c.comp (sphericalClasses _ 1).subtype).ker ≤
    (ω.comp (sphericalClasses _ 1).subtype).ker)
  (hc : c.comp (sphericalClasses _ 1).subtype ≠ 0)
  (h : 0 < PeriodGroup.chern _ _ (projectiveSpaceGenerator ω c v hn))
include h

/-- **On `CPⁿ` with positive Chern number of the generator, the generator is the positive Chern
generator** of the period group: its integer coordinate is `1`. So its minimal Chern number is
`c ℓ`, which is `n + 1` for the first Chern class of `CPⁿ`. -/
theorem chernEquivInt_projectiveSpaceGenerator :
    chernEquivInt hker hc (projectiveSpaceGenerator ω c v hn) = 1 :=
  chernEquivInt_eq_one_of_zmultiples_eq_top hker hc (zmultiples_projectiveSpaceGenerator v hn) h

/-- On `CPⁿ` with positive Chern number of the generator, the Laurent exponent of the generator
is `-1`: the Laurent variable is `e^(-ℓ)`. -/
theorem laurentExponent_projectiveSpaceGenerator :
    laurentExponent hker hc (projectiveSpaceGenerator ω c v hn) = -1 :=
  laurentExponent_eq_neg_one_of_zmultiples_eq_top hker hc (zmultiples_projectiveSpaceGenerator v hn)
    h

end Laurent

/-- **The generator is the class of a projective line.** On `CPⁿ⁺¹`, with the base point
`[e₁] = [0 : 1 : 0 : ⋯ : 0]`, the generator `ℓ` is the class of the coordinate line
`TauCeti.ComplexProjectiveSpace.lineSquare n`, the sphere `[1 : z : 0 : ⋯ : 0]`
(`TauCeti.ComplexProjectiveSpace.pi2MulEquivInt_symm_ofAdd_one`). So its periods are the values
of `ω` and `c` on the class of that line; for the Fubini–Study form and the first Chern class
these are its area and its first Chern number. -/
theorem projectiveSpaceGenerator_eq_ofHomotopyGroup_lineSquare
    {ω : ((singularHomologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{0} ℤ) 2).obj (ModuleCat.of ℤ ℤ)).obj
      (TopCat.of (ComplexProjectiveSpace (n + 1))) →+ ℝ}
    {c : ((singularHomologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{0} ℤ) 2).obj (ModuleCat.of ℤ ℤ)).obj
      (TopCat.of (ComplexProjectiveSpace (n + 1))) →+ ℤ} :
    projectiveSpaceGenerator ω c (affineUnitVector 1 0) n.add_one_ne_zero =
      ofHomotopyGroup ω c (affineParam 1 0) (Additive.ofMul ⟦lineSquare n⟧) := by
  rw [projectiveSpaceGenerator_def, pi2MulEquivInt_symm_ofAdd_one, lineClass_def]
  exact ofHomotopyGroup_map_id _ _

end SphericalPeriodGroup

open SphericalPeriodGroup

variable (v : sphere (0 : EuclideanSpace ℂ (Fin (n + 1))) 1) (hn : n ≠ 0)

/-- **Recapping by the generator in the Laurent model.** On `CPⁿ` with positive area and Chern
number of the generator, the Laurent coordinates of the Floer Novikov ring send the monomial
`e^(-k ℓ)` to `X^k`: the Laurent variable `X` is `e^(-ℓ)`. -/
theorem NovikovRing.toLaurentSeries_single_neg_zsmul_projectiveSpaceGenerator {R : Type*}
    [Semiring R] {τ : ℝ} (hτ' : ∀ s, ω.comp (sphericalClasses _ 1).subtype s =
      τ * c.comp (sphericalClasses _ 1).subtype s)
    (hc : c.comp (sphericalClasses _ 1).subtype ≠ 0) (hτ : 0 < τ)
    (h : 0 < PeriodGroup.chern _ _ (projectiveSpaceGenerator ω c v hn)) (k : ℤ) (r : R) :
    NovikovRing.toLaurentSeries hτ' hc hτ (single (-(k • projectiveSpaceGenerator ω c v hn)) r) =
      HahnSeries.single k r :=
  NovikovRing.toLaurentSeries_single_neg_zsmul hτ' hc hτ (zmultiples_projectiveSpaceGenerator v hn)
    h k r

/-- **The coefficient comparison on `CPⁿ` is bijective.** Unless both periods of the generator
vanish, the comparison `q^A ↦ e^(-[A])` from the Novikov ring indexed by the class group
`H₂(CPⁿ; ℤ)` of genus-zero Gromov–Witten theory to the Floer Novikov ring is bijective, since the
class map `SphericalPeriodGroup.ofSingularHomology` is an isomorphism `H₂(CPⁿ; ℤ) ≅ Γ`
(`SphericalPeriodGroup.ofSingularHomology_projectiveSpace_bijective`). -/
theorem coefficientComparison_ofSingularHomology_projectiveSpace_bijective {R : Type*} [Semiring R]
    (h : PeriodGroup.area _ _ (projectiveSpaceGenerator ω c v hn) ≠ 0 ∨
      PeriodGroup.chern _ _ (projectiveSpaceGenerator ω c v hn) ≠ 0) :
    Function.Bijective (coefficientComparison (R := R)
      (ofSingularHomology ω c (sphericalClasses_eq_top_of_simplyConnectedSpace _))
      (area_ofSingularHomology (sphericalClasses_eq_top_of_simplyConnectedSpace _))) :=
  ⟨coefficientComparison_injective _ _ (ofSingularHomology_projectiveSpace_bijective v hn h).1,
    coefficientComparison_surjective _ _ (ofSingularHomology_surjective _)⟩

/-- **The comparison `q^A ↦ e^(-A)` in Laurent coordinates on `CPⁿ`.** With positive area and
Chern number of the generator, the comparison out of the Novikov ring indexed by `H₂(CPⁿ; ℤ)` sends
the monomial `q^(k [ℓ])` to the Laurent monomial `X^k`. For `k = 1` this is `q^ℓ ↦ X`, the
class `q^[line]` of the quantum relation of `CPⁿ`: on `CPⁿ⁺¹`, based at `[e₁]`, `ℓ` is the class
of the coordinate line with its complex orientation
(`SphericalPeriodGroup.projectiveSpaceGenerator_eq_ofHomotopyGroup_lineSquare`). -/
theorem NovikovRing.toLaurentSeries_coefficientComparison_projectiveSpace_single {R : Type*}
    [Semiring R] {τ : ℝ} (hτ' : ∀ s, ω.comp (sphericalClasses _ 1).subtype s =
      τ * c.comp (sphericalClasses _ 1).subtype s)
    (hc : c.comp (sphericalClasses _ 1).subtype ≠ 0) (hτ : 0 < τ)
    (h : 0 < PeriodGroup.chern _ _ (projectiveSpaceGenerator ω c v hn)) (k : ℤ) (r : R) :
    NovikovRing.toLaurentSeries hτ' hc hτ
        (coefficientComparison
          (ofSingularHomology ω c (sphericalClasses_eq_top_of_simplyConnectedSpace _))
          (area_ofSingularHomology (sphericalClasses_eq_top_of_simplyConnectedSpace _))
          (single (k • hurewiczIntHom _ (mk n v) 1
            (Additive.ofMul ((pi2MulEquivInt v hn).symm (Multiplicative.ofAdd 1)))) r)) =
      HahnSeries.single k r := by
  rw [coefficientComparison_single, map_zsmul,
    ofSingularHomology_hurewiczIntHom_pi2MulEquivInt_symm]
  exact NovikovRing.toLaurentSeries_single_neg_zsmul_projectiveSpaceGenerator v hn hτ' hc hτ h k r

/-- **The raw degrees of Floer monomials on `CPⁿ`.** A nonzero monomial `r e^(k ℓ)` of the Floer
Novikov ring has raw degree `2 c(k ℓ) = 2 k c(ℓ)` and no other. -/
theorem NovikovRing.single_zsmul_projectiveSpaceGenerator_mem_gradeBy_degree_iff {R : Type*}
    [Semiring R] {r : R} (hr : r ≠ 0) (k d : ℤ) :
    single (k • projectiveSpaceGenerator ω c v hn) r ∈
        gradeBy R (-PeriodGroup.area _ _) (PeriodGroup.degree _ _) d ↔
      d = 2 * k * PeriodGroup.chern _ _ (projectiveSpaceGenerator ω c v hn) := by
  rw [single_mem_gradeBy_iff hr, PeriodGroup.degree_eq_two_smul_chern,
    (single_mem_gradeBy_iff hr).1
      (single_zsmul_mem_gradeBy_two_smul (N := -PeriodGroup.area _ _) _ k _ r), eq_comm]

/-- **The comparison `q^A ↦ e^(-A)` preserves the degree of the quantum relation of `CPⁿ`.**
Let `L ∈ H₂(CPⁿ; ℤ)` be the Hurewicz class of the generator of `π₂(CPⁿ)`. The comparison sends the
quantum monomial `q^(k L)`, of degree `2 c(k L) = 2 k c(L)`, to `e^(-k ℓ)`, of raw Floer degree
`-2 k c(L)`, that is of cochain degree `2 k c(L)` in the grading `C^k = CF_(n-k)`. When `c` is the
first Chern number and `L` the class of a line, `c(L) = n + 1`; for `k = 1` the coefficient `q^L`
of the quantum relation `x^(⋆(n+1)) = q^L · 1` and its image `e^(-ℓ)` both have degree `2 n + 2`,
the degree of `x^(n+1)`. -/
theorem coefficientComparison_projectiveSpace_single_mem_gradeBy_degree {R : Type*} [Semiring R]
    (k : ℤ) (r : R) :
    coefficientComparison
        (ofSingularHomology ω c (sphericalClasses_eq_top_of_simplyConnectedSpace _))
        (area_ofSingularHomology (sphericalClasses_eq_top_of_simplyConnectedSpace _))
        (single (k • hurewiczIntHom _ (mk n v) 1
          (Additive.ofMul ((pi2MulEquivInt v hn).symm (Multiplicative.ofAdd 1)))) r) ∈
      gradeBy R (-PeriodGroup.area _ _) (PeriodGroup.degree _ _)
        (-(2 * k * c (hurewiczIntHom _ (mk n v) 1
          (Additive.ofMul ((pi2MulEquivInt v hn).symm (Multiplicative.ofAdd 1)))))) := by
  rw [PeriodGroup.degree_eq_two_smul_chern]
  exact coefficientComparison_mem_gradeBy_two_smul _ _ c _ (chern_ofSingularHomology _)
    (single_zsmul_mem_gradeBy_two_smul c k _ r)

namespace SphericalCapClass

variable {x : ComplexProjectiveSpace n} {γ : Ω (ComplexProjectiveSpace n) x}

/-- **Recapping on `CPⁿ`.** Unless both periods of the generator vanish, any two cap classes of a
loop in `CPⁿ` differ by recapping with a unique multiple of the generator. -/
theorem existsUnique_zsmul_projectiveSpaceGenerator_vadd_eq
    (h : PeriodGroup.area _ _ (projectiveSpaceGenerator ω c v hn) ≠ 0 ∨
      PeriodGroup.chern _ _ (projectiveSpaceGenerator ω c v hn) ≠ 0)
    (D D' : SphericalCapClass ω c γ) :
    ∃! k : ℤ, k • projectiveSpaceGenerator ω c v hn +ᵥ D = D' :=
  existsUnique_zsmul_vadd_eq (zmultiples_projectiveSpaceGenerator v hn) (ofHomotopyGroup_ne_zero h)
    D D'

end SphericalCapClass

end TauCeti.Floer
